<title>USA: US high-ylds seen armored against weaker cash flow.</title>
<headline>US high-ylds seen armored against weaker cash flow.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Negative cash flows of U.S. high-yield mutual funds in the latest week are not expected to upend demand for the mounting slate of new issues, money managers said.</p>
<p>Many new deals this week have posted better-than-expected demand, managers said, reflecting coffers still brimming with cash looking for bonds. That, they said, lessens the impact the $31.6 million in outflows from funds recorded by AMG Data Services in the week ended May 28.</p>
</text>
